  "notes": [
    "-ER verb with spelling change: g→j before a/o (to preserve the soft /x/ sound)",
    "Only the **yo Presente** is affected in indicative tenses: **cojo**",
    "All other indicative forms keep the g (coges, coge, cogemos, cogen, cogí, etc.)",
    "The g→j change applies throughout the present subjunctive (coja, cojas, etc.)",
    "Past participle: cogido",
    "Very common in Spain for \"to take\" transport: coger el autobús/metro/tren",
    "Note: \"coger\" has vulgar connotations in Latin America — use \"agarrar\" or \"tomar\" there"
  ],
